NEARS-3239 — VendorController@view tab-scope safelist — live QA HTTP transcript
Server under test: this worktree's own `php artisan serve` (port 8130), DB = shared local
dev `multi_food_db` (read-only — no rows written; auth established by minting an in-process
Laravel session for an EXISTING admin row, matching login_remember_token so AdminMiddleware
accepts it, with zero writes to the admins/admin_roles tables).

Actors (pre-existing seeded fixtures, found already present in the local dev DB):
  - admin id=1  admin@admin.com        role_id=1 (Master admin / super admin)
  - admin id=4  qa.role.c@nears-qa.test role_id=4, AdminRole modules=["withdraw_list"], zone_id=2

Store used: id=10 "Eorange", zone_id=2 (store id=1 is a DIFFERENT zone and is filtered out of
this zoned admin's ZoneScope — a pre-existing, unrelated zoning behavior, not a defect of this
ticket; switched to a same-zone store once discovered).

== AC1 — withdraw_list-only denied on a non-disbursement tab ==
GET /admin/transactions/store/view/10/conversations  (session: qa.role.c, withdraw_list only)
  -> HTTP 302 (Toastr deny + back(), not the conversations view)
Followed redirect target body contains:
  `<script type="text/javascript">toastr.error('Access denied','');</script>`
  and no store-conversation content — generic deny toast only, no tab content leaked.

== AC2 — withdraw_list-only reaches null tab and disbursements tab ==
GET /admin/transactions/store/view/10                (no tab)
  -> HTTP 200, <title>Eorange</title>  (admin-views.vendor.view.index)
GET /admin/transactions/store/view/10/disbursements
  -> HTTP 200, body contains "Disbursement"/"Withdraw" (admin-views.vendor.view.disbursement)

== AC3 mechanism — sibling admin.store.view route unaffected (zero code touched) ==
GET /admin/store/view/10/business_plan                (session: super admin, id=1, role_id=1)
  -> HTTP 200, body contains "Business Plan"/"Subscription"/"Package"
     (admin-views.vendor.view.subscription) — super admin's role_id==1 bypass in
     Helpers::module_permission_check is exercised live and reaches every tab unchanged.
GET /admin/store/view/10/business_plan                (session: qa.role.c, withdraw_list only)
  -> HTTP 302 (module:store route-level gate still enforced — this diff touched zero code on
     this route; the pre-existing gate for a non-store-holding role is intact).

== Additional QA point — status-filter unaffected by this fix ==
POST /admin/transactions/store/status-filter  withdraw_status_filter=approved
  (session: qa.role.c, withdraw_list only, same module.any:account,withdraw_list route gate)
  -> HTTP 200, body: "approved"  (unchanged session-filter echo, VendorController@view not
     involved in this endpoint at all)

== Regression spot checks (unrelated admin pages, super admin session) ==
GET /admin                    -> HTTP 200 <title>Nears</title> (dashboard)
GET /admin/store/list         -> HTTP 200 <title>Store List</title>
GET /admin/customer/list      -> HTTP 200 <title>Customer List</title>

== Logs-first check ==
`Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log` — no new [FAIL]/[ERR]/exception entries during this live
session's requests (grepped the request time window); the only recent entries are from this
worktree's OWN `vendor/bin/phpunit --filter "Nears3239VendorViewTabScopeTest|AdminModuleGateTest"`
run (43/43 green, independently re-run by QA, not just relayed from the engineer).

== Data DoR gap (documented, not silently skipped) ==
No pre-existing local-DB fixture holds account-only, store-only, withdraw_list+store,
withdraw_list+report, or withdraw_list+customer_management. Per the standing read-only-DB hard
rule (no raw DML / ad-hoc AdminRole rows without an approved, versioned seeder), QA did not
create these. Those five scenarios are covered by
`Admin/tests/Feature/Security/Nears3239VendorViewTabScopeTest.php`
(test_account_only_is_denied_on_conversations_tab,
test_account_only_reaches_{null,disbursements}_tab,
test_withdraw_list_plus_{store,report,customer_management}_role_reaches_conversations_tab,
test_store_only_role_reaches_business_plan_tab_via_sibling_route) — all passing, independently
re-run above, and asserting via Laravel's TestResponse (full HTTP-kernel + real
routing/middleware/controller dispatch), not a bare unit test.
